# App rules — <app> (TEMPLATE)

Copy this file to `rules/<app>.md` (gitignored, like your `configs/<app>.json`)
and replace the examples below with your app's real rules. Point your config's
`target.rulesFile` (and optionally `platforms.<p>.rulesFile`) at it.

The spoke re-reads these EVERY turn, so keep them dense. Only put here what the
spoke can't get elsewhere: don't restate a tool's own description (`read_creds`,
`app cold-reset`, etc. already tell the spoke what they do), and leave
device-input rules (e.g. how a focused field is SUBMITTED) on the DeviceProfile.
Each rule must be true and stand alone.

## <quirk title — the negative nuance a tool won't state>
Capture what a tool's description leaves implied. Example:

> A plain force-stop leaves the AuthKit session intact. Use `app cold-reset` for
> a true signed-out first run before testing sign-in.

## <quirk title — a behavior the spoke can't derive by observing>
Write it as a procedure, with the failure mode. Example:

> Focusing any text field docks a NEW input above the keyboard, so the `@ref`
> from your last `observe` is STALE; typing into it silently does the wrong thing
> (no crash, so no guard catches it). Enter text as: `tap` → `observe` again →
> `type` into the newly-docked `@ref`, never the original.
